---
import { SITE } from '../site';
---

<section aria-label={`About ${SITE.name}`} class="mx-auto max-w-[90rem] px-5 pt-28 sm:px-10 lg:pt-36">
  <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-x-10">
    <p class="reveal text-[length:var(--text-title)] leading-[1.1] tracking-[-0.02em] lg:col-span-6">
      Keep the distro you trust. Make every machine on it yours.
    </p>
    <div class="text-body leading-relaxed text-soft lg:col-span-5 lg:col-start-8 lg:pt-2">
      <p class="reveal" style="--d: 70ms">
        With FormalSpec, you describe each machine in Starlark, including its packages, files, services, and the distro
        underneath. A single lockfile pins every version, so machines on the same commit run the same software.
      </p>
      <p class="reveal mt-5" style="--d: 140ms">
        The installer sets up a new disk from that description. NativeDesktop apps and FormalShell make it feel like one
        desktop from the moment you sign in.
      </p>
      <p class="reveal mt-5" style="--d: 210ms">
        <a class="link inline-block py-2 text-ink" href={SITE.github}>Browse the code on GitHub</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
